      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Since $n$ is divided by 6 with a remainder of 1, we can write $n$ as $n = 6k + 1$ for some integer $k$.\nWhen we add 2010 to $n$, we get $n + 2010 = 6k + 1 + 2010 = 6k + 2011$.\nNow, when we divide $n + 2010$ by 6, the remainder is the same as the remainder when 2011 is divided by 6.\nSince $2011 = 6 \\cdot 335 + 1$, the remainder when 2011 is divided by 6 is 1.\nTherefore, the remainder when $n + 2010$ is divided by 6 is also 1.\n$\\boxed{1}$",
